  "body": "What happens: CamCraft has one Sodick wire post, \"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)\". It writes the 1998 Mark 21 word set, including taper as `G74/G75` with `U V`. The current Sodick LN1W/LN2W controls (AQ400L, AQ600L) program taper as `G51`/`G52` with `A` and cancel with `G50`, with `TP`/`TN` for the table heights (Sodick LN1W/LN2W operation manual, Sodick Inc. 2012). A user with an LN2W machine who picks our only Sodick post gets taper words their control does not read the way the program means. The header only says \"NOT VERIFIED ON A CONTROL\"; it does not say which control the words are for.\n\nFound when a Sodick AQ600L / LN2W owner dry-ran our kit (2026-11-25, see #1500).\n\nExpected: the post's header (and its description in the post list) names the control it targets and states that LN1W/LN2W taper is not supported; a taper cut posted with this post states the same in its header next to the first taper word. Until the LN2W dialect (#4045) exists, that is a visible refusal-style warning instead of a silent mismatch.\n\nDone means: every program from the Mark 21 post carries a header line naming the Mark 21 control and \"LN1W/LN2W: not supported - taper words differ\"; taper programs repeat it beside the first G74/G75; the post list description says the same; goldens updated; no motion or code line changes.\n\nRefs #4045, #1500, #617.\n",
